      "seed": 285172012,
      "version": 711,
      "versionNonce": 1041759508,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1779711707775,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "16 is the [0001 0000] binary,\nbut in decimal representation.\nSo every index in rows array is\na row, and its number\nrepresents the decimal form of\nthe seen numbers, as\nconverting them to base 2\n(binary), we can check if a\nnumber has been seen based on\nits binary representation.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "16 is the [0001 0000] binary, but in decimal representation. So every index in rows array is a row, and its number represents the decimal form of the seen numbers, as converting them to base 2 (binary), we can check if a number has been seen based on its binary representation.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
